# KNOWN idiom debt, one site per line. This file only ever
# SHRINKS: no tool path adds to it. A finding is fixed in the
# code, or annotated `// LICENSED <name>: reason` at the site —
# a `native:` finding reads no license of its own (a rule
# carries no comment of its own), so a `// LICENSED` comment
# beside one is the reader's documentation, never a
# suppression this tool honours: what sits below is either a
# RULE MATCHING ITS OWN QUOTE PATTERN (compiler/idioms.av's
# declarations — a structural artifact, since a pattern
# necessarily spells the shape it detects) or genuinely
# accepted debt, reviewed at adoption and every time after.
# `make idioms-accept` prunes what is gone. Burn it down.
